UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Nine of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "The Resilience Threshold"—the final, grueling stage of the sovereign’s journey through the Suit of Wands, where the individual, having weathered the high-velocity storms and the chaotic frictions of the previous phases, reaches a state of profound, hardened endurance. Moving beyond the frantic speed of the Eight, the Nine signifies the phase of "Tactical Perseverance," where the consciousness is no longer reacting to the field, but is operating from a state of total, stoic readiness. Visually depicted as a battered, wounded, yet alert figure standing before a defensive palisade of eight staves, holding a ninth as a weapon, this archetype embodies the concept of "Cognitive Fortitude"—the understanding that you have survived the worst of the volatility and that your victory is now contingent only on your refusal to collapse. Within the complex architecture of your consciousness, this is the stage of "systemic hardening," where the repeated pressures of your evolutionary journey have transmuted your egoic armor into a reliable, high-integrity structure. When the Nine of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Last Stand" status; you are near the conclusion of a significant cycle of manifestation, and the final obstacles are often the most deceptive, appearing as a cumulative fatigue that threatens to break your focus just as you reach the finish line. This card commands you to bypass the physiological and psychological signals of burnout by anchoring yourself in the absolute, non-negotiable truth of your original mission. You are being tasked with the essential work of "strategic grit": you must conserve your energy, trust the defensive framework you have built, and refuse to surrender to the temptation of "just letting go" before the objective is fully locked. To inhabit the Nine of Wands is to master the art of "sovereign tenacity," recognizing that your current weariness is not a sign of defeat, but a testament to the magnitude of the threshold you are currently crossing. It is the ultimate validation that your commitment to your soul-intent has been tested at every level, and that by choosing to remain standing, you have successfully integrated the power of the Wands into the very fabric of your being, preparing you for the final, concluding mastery of the Ten.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Nine of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic exhaustion," "defensive fragility," or the catastrophic breakdown of your internal resilience—a state where the weight of your past struggles has finally compromised your ability to function in the present. The reversal suggests that you have been holding onto a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script of "fighting to the end" for so long that you have become fundamentally brittle, unable to distinguish between genuine, necessary struggle and the reflexive, low-vibration repetition of your own trauma. You are essentially "fighting a war that is already over," running a high-maintenance protocol that prioritizes the preservation of your "hardened" persona over the actual, living reality of your present-day needs. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "survivor," while internally, you are paralyzed by a profound, gnawing sense of defeat, leading to a state of chronic defensive posture, hypersensitivity to perceived threats, and a persistent, gnawing sense that you are on the verge of a total, structural collapse. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of paranoia"; you are obsessively scanning the horizon for the next blow, refusing to acknowledge that the only real threat to your stability at this stage is your own refusal to lower your shield and rest. The reversed Nine of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of being truly vulnerable, and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop your weapon and admit to your own, profound humanity, you would lose the only identity you have left. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these weary, defensive scripts, perform a brutal audit of your current "battlefield," and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to acknowledge that the siege has ended. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance struggle, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, authentic peace. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of surrender—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the fight over the victory, and realizing that until you are willing to set down the staff and accept the reality of your own, earned sanctuary, you will continue to be starved by the very battle you have worked so hard to win.'
WHERE id = 23;
